   "title": "Handling Intermittent and Unclassified Customer Reports",
   "content_summary": "Guidance on triaging tickets with vague symptoms like data mismatches or inconsistent browser behavior where the root cause is not immediately apparent.",
   "content_body": "When facing intermittent failures or unclassified issues, first gather detailed reproduction steps and environment metadata to rule out operator error. If the issue persists across different browsers or devices without a clear pattern, check for unsupported configurations in the customer's deployment. Use internal tools to compare backend logs against frontend timestamps to identify data mismatches. If standard troubleshooting fails, escalate to engineering with a summary of the inconsistent behavior and any captured HAR files. Often, these cases require a configuration change or additional customer education on supported environments."
